(Berthelsen et al. 2018 ; Van der Linden and Palmieri 2022) . While the GUREGT (Berthelsen et al. 2018) has been developed, this guideline only offers a generic approach for reporting all three different GT approaches: Classic (or Glasserian), Straussian, and Constructivist (Birks and Mills 2022) . A ratified guideline specific to Classic GT has yet to be established. The use of generic GT or Ql guidelines to report Classic GT studies may contribute to the omission of methodological nuances unique to Classic GT, such as identifying the main concern, which sets it apart from other GT approaches. Such omissions cause readers to question the study's methodological rigour, potentially compromising the integrity of Classic GT outcomes. How nursing researchers adhere to the methodological criteria of Classic GT has not been reported.
