- The Pennsylvania State Board of Cosmetology nail technician (manicurist) Theory/Procedural Skills Examination is created and scored by Pearson VUE and contains 75 multiple-choice items: 60 scored items (50 general and 10 state) plus 15 unmarked pretest items (10 general and 5 state) that do not affect the score.
- The time limit is 1 hour 45 minutes, the examination has no hands-on practical, and the computer exam is offered in English, Korean, Spanish, Vietnamese, and Chinese (Simplified).
- The February 2026 content outline weights Rules, Regulations, and Safety at 30% to 40%, Nail Structure and Nail Analysis at 15% to 20%, Professional Services at 30% to 40%, and Nail Enhancements at 12% to 18%.
...
The credential in this guide is the Pennsylvania nail technician license, a limited license under the Cosmetology Law. Statutory language still says manicurist. On this path, nail technician and manicurist name the same limited license. They do not name the full cosmetologist license. The examination is the Theory/Procedural Skills Examination of the Pennsylvania State Board of Cosmetology. Pearson VUE creates that examination and scores it.

Two documents fix the facts in this section. Operational rules come from the Pennsylvania Cosmetology Candidate Handbook dated August 2026. Domain weights come from the content outline current as of February 2026. OpenExamPrep publishes this chapter as an independent study guide for people preparing for that examination. The Board did not write these pages.

