## Freelance Video Editing Rates in India 

Indian freelance video editors offer distinct competitive advantages. High skill levels paired with affordable pricing make India a hub for creators and companies aiming for cost-efficiency without quality compromise.

- Basic editing projects: For short videos (2-5 minutes), including simple cutting, trimming, transitions, and light corrections, Indian freelancers typically charge between ₹1,000 to ₹3,000 per video. These services cater to startups, small businesses, and social media content creators.
- Intermediate projects: Videos with advanced editing needs such as multi-layer timelines, color grading, visual effects, and audio enhancements fall within ₹3,000 to ₹10,000 range. This category suits marketing teams, YouTubers wanting polished content, and educators.
- Social media and branded content: Popular social media formats with subtitles, captions, and fast-paced edits are charged from ₹2,000 to ₹5,000 each, balancing engagement with budget.
- Corporate videos and brand films: These projects require a professional finesse in storytelling, animation, voiceover integration, and branding elements, priced between ₹5,000 to ₹15,000 per video. Corporates and agencies represent key clients here.
- Long-form projects: Documentaries, event coverage, and specialized films command premium fees, ₹15,000 to ₹50,000+, reflecting time-consuming editing, research, and narrative crafting.
- Motion graphics & animation: Depending on complexity and length, these services range from ₹5,000 up to ₹25,000 or more, often bundled with editing packages for high-impact content.
- Monthly retainer packages: Regular clients needing ongoing video editing (10-30 videos monthly) can negotiate retainers from ₹25,000 to ₹1,50,000+, offering stable wo…

