URL: https://wevion.ai/en/blog/lead-ads-vs-landing-page-which-converts-better/
The lead ads vs landing page debate is one of the most consequential decisions in Facebook advertising. Both approaches generate leads, but they do it through fundamentally different mechanisms that affect volume, cost, quality, and downstream conversion rates. Choosing the wrong one does not just waste ad budget — it wastes your sales team's time on leads that never close.

Quick answer: Lead ads usually win on volume and cost-per-lead because the native form removes friction, while landing pages win on lead quality and downstream close rates because they pre-qualify and let you capture richer data. The right choice depends on your sales motion: high-volume nurture favors lead ads; high-ticket, sales-led funnels favor landing pages.

This comparison goes beyond surface-level conversion rates. With mobile accounting for the large majority of Facebook ad impressions (Statista, 2024), the friction of a separate landing-page load is a real variable in this decision, not a footnote. We break down how each approach performs across the entire funnel — from initial click to closed deal — so you can make an informed decision based on your specific business model and sales process.
