Cedar Fair operates 13 theme parks in the U.S. and three in California (Knott's Berry Farm, California's Great America and Gilroy Gardens.) Nearly all their parks offer a Halloween event. Knott's Scary Farm was operating its haunt before it was acquired by Cedar Fair and the mega-theme park corporation has wisely borrowed elements of this highly-successful annual festival of the macabre to make their localized events such as CA's Great American Haunt and Pumpkin Fest popular with both adults and kids. With Peanuts & Snoopy cartoon characters part of their brand, Halloween is a natural, and the kids' events are fun for both youngsters and adults.

