Accessibility is often measured by whether content works—not how hard it is to use. This session introduces an evolved Screen Reader Ropes Course framework for evaluating cognitive load in screen reader navigation across web and PDF environments. Participants will learn how technically compliant experiences can still create unnecessary effort, and how to design and test for efficiency, clarity, and real usability in higher education contexts.
