This research focuses on how users respond to implicit confirmation in a spoken language system. With implicit confirmation, the computer asks the user a question and then takes the answer and incorporates it into the next question. This technique allows a spoken language system to verify a user's responses. However, few systems use implicit confirmation because there is no general understanding of how users respond during this type of dialogue. This research is an attempt to study the types of responses a user gives when a system uses implicit confirmation.
