Nasdaq Stock Market Rules, Regulation, IM-5101-2., Nasdaq, Listing of
Companies Whose Business Plan is to Complete One or More Acquisitions

Click to open document in a browser

Generally, Nasdaq will not permit the initial or continued listing of a Company that has no speciﬁc business plan
or that has indicated that its business plan is to engage in a merger or acquisition with an unidentiﬁed company
or companies.

However, in the case of a Company whose business plan is to complete an initial public oﬀering and engage in a
