FutureMeds operates as a dedicated site network organization facilitating patient-centric clinical trials across Europe. The company was founded in 2020 by Radek Janiak. Its business model revolves around providing comprehensive site and Decentralized Clinical Trial (DCT) solutions to major pharmaceutical companies and Contract Research Organizations (CROs). By managing a network of strategically located research sites, FutureMeds aims to streamline the clinical trial process, enhance patient recruitment and retention, and ensure the delivery of high-quality data. This approach helps to accelerate the development and approval of new medical treatments.

The company's service portfolio includes end-to-end trial management, leveraging its network of over 27 sites in 7 countries, more than 220 investigators, and a substantial force of over 1400 homecare providers. This infrastructure supports a range of therapeutic areas and enables both traditional site-based trials and decentralized models where some or all trial activities occur at a participant's home. FutureMeds generates revenue by charging its clients, the sponsors and CROs, for these clinical trial services. The company has demonstrated significant growth, having acquired or opened multiple research sites across countries like Poland, Germany, Spain, and Ukraine, and reported a 280% revenue increase in 2022.

