Electrophysiology studies are low-risk procedures used to examine how the heart’s electrical system is working. By inserting thin wires through a vein and guiding them to the heart, doctors can evaluate how electrical signals move through the heart and identify any irregular rhythms or conduction issues. For patients diagnosed with SVT, catheter ablation offers a minimally invasive, often curative treatment option. The procedure uses targeted energy to safely eliminate the tissue causing the irregular rhythm.

Part of our Cardiology services at St Andrew’s Toowoomba Hospital.

