at St Andrew’s
...
A cardioversion procedure aims to restore the heart’s normal rhythm from an abnormal rhythm using high-energy shocks. Most cardioversions are performed to treat certain types of irregular heartbeats (arrhythmias), including atrial fibrillation. 
- ### Electrophysiology Studies (EPS) 

An Electrophysiology Study (EPS) is a minimally invasive procedure used to diagnose arrhythmias. During the procedure, small catheters are inserted through a vein and threaded to the heart, where they record electrical signals. Providing complex 3D electroanatomical mapping of cardiac arrhythmias, this test allows our heart specialists to pinpoint the exact source of the arrhythmia and determine the best course of action for treatment. 
- ### Radiofrequency ablation 

Radiofrequency energy (heat) or cryoablation (cold) is used to cause a small scar in an area of the heart electrical system identified during EPS as the site of an abnormal heart rhythm, resulting in a break in that circuit. RFA may be undertaken when medications fail to control an abnormal heart rhythm.
