- The total annual revenues generated in the EU27 from the auctions and then allocated to EU Member States has more than tripled between 2020 and 2023, to reach 33 billion Euros. However, the total revenue generated in the EU27 in 2024 decreased by 26% compared to 2023, reaching 24.3 billion Euros, due to a drop in the EUAs prices and a larger share of the overall revenues allocated to the Modernisation Fund, the Innovation Fund and the Recovery and Resilience Facility funds.
- Between 2013-2022, nearly 75% of the auctioning revenues were used by Member States for climate and energy related purposes.
