Verified April 2026 - BentoML 1.1.0+ coldstart patterns are correct. Critical addition: readinessProbe.initialDelaySeconds must account for GPU warmup time, not just model load time; nvidiasmi in init_containers adds 25 seconds.

Set initialDelaySeconds to max(measured_cold_start + 10s, 45s) to avoid probe failures masking actual timeouts. The article correctly notes initialDelaySeconds is a hard deadline, but doesn't mention that liveness and readiness probes must differ: use readinessProbe.initialDelaySeconds=45+ and livenessProbe.initialDelaySeconds=60+ to prevent premature pod eviction during legitimate slow startups.

For multiGPU setups, resources={'gpu': 1} in @bentoml.service() reserves exactly one GPU; if your Kubernetes node has 4 GPUs but you only reserve 1, the other 3 remain idle for other workloads-intentional but easy to miss. Measure actual cold start via: time bentoml serve bentoml_service:SentimentAnalysis port 3000, then grep logs for 'Model loaded' to find the true duration before adding your probe buffer.
