SQM has two production facilities at the salar. To mine the potassium and lithium salts, large amounts of brine are pumped to the surface by wells. The pumped brine is conveyed via canals and directed into the large, lined evaporation ponds. Clouds rarely form or persist over this region, and the area is extremely windy, providing an ideal environment to evaporate the large amounts of water required to deliver the brine into the ponds.
