## Battery-grade vs technical-grade

Battery-grade chemicals carry tight limits (parts per million) on sodium, potassium, calcium, magnesium, iron, sulfate, chloride and magnetic particles, because impurities degrade cathode performance. Exact limits are set in each supply contract; China’s industry standard YS/T 582 (battery-grade lithium carbonate) and national standard GB/T 11075 (lithium carbonate) are common references. Technical-grade material is cheaper and used where purity matters less.
