Direct lithium extraction (DLE), in contrast, offers a more efficient and sustainable way to extract lithium from salars or basins. In DLE, the brine is processed through separation modules where lithium is selectively removed with recovery rates of up to 90%. The extracted lithium is then sent to a downstream plant to be converted into Li 2 CO 3. This process eliminates the need for large land areas and lengthy evaporation times. It also enables water recovery from the brine, reducing both land and water usage, making DLE a more sustainable solution.
