[3] Cold boxes and vaccine carriers
URL: https://extranet.who.int/prequal/sites/default/files/media_document/e004_0.pdf
The category E004 includes cold boxes, vaccine carriers and other passive, insulated containers used primarily for the transport and sometimes for the temporary storage of vaccines. Passive devices are non-powered devices that use ice-packs or other thermal storage materials to control the temperature of the vaccine compartment. Details regarding the products included in each sub-category of E004, as well as guidelines, performance specifications and verification protocols for this category, can be accessed through the drop-down sections below.

### E004.1: Choosing a cold box or vaccine carrier

End-users of insulated containers and their procurement agents are advised to consider the 
following points when choosing vaccine storage equipment from this category: 
Vaccine storage capacity: Vaccine storage capacity of each product is detailed on the 
