[5] Debit Purchase and Contactless Limits in Canada by Bank (2026) (2026-06-03T08:43:58.000Z)
URL: https://wealthnorth.ca/banking/limits/debit-card-limits-canada/
## Contactless (tap) limits

Interac sets the ceiling for a tap payment with an Interac debit card: up to $250 per transaction, with a cumulative contactless limit that each bank or credit union sets on top. Once the cumulative tap spending reaches the bank’s figure, the terminal asks for the card to be inserted with the PIN, which resets the count.

So the per-tap amount on your card is your bank’s choice up to $250, and a store can set a lower tap amount on its own terminals. Desjardins, for example, publishes its tap limits: $250 per transaction and $1,000 per day. Purchases over the tap limit still go through with chip and PIN, up to the daily purchase limit above.
