Enterprise Okta Workforce Identity deals of 1,000+ users typically achieve 25 to 35% off list pricing. Deals combining Workforce Identity with Customer Identity (CIAM) and Privileged Access achieve 32 to 42% bundle discounts. The highest discounts come from multi-year commitments (3-year) paired with competitive evaluations, organizations benchmarking Okta against Microsoft Entra ID or CyberArk consistently achieve the top of the range.

How does Okta's per-user pricing model work at enterprise scale?

Okta pricing is primarily per monthly active user (MAU) for CIAM and per user per month for Workforce Identity. Enterprise contracts move to annual committed volume with tiered pricing. The key negotiating point is defining 'users', Okta's default definition can include service accounts and applications, dramatically inflating unit counts. Our benchmark data shows 18 to 28% of enterprise Okta spend is attributable to non-human identities that can be repriced or excluded through contract negotiation.

