[3] MOVUS Review: Pricing, Features & Verdict - Softwr
URL: https://www.softwr.com/software/movus
As of 1 September 2026, MOVUS's pricing is not published; the vendor quotes on request. MOVUS sells FitMachine as a hardware plus subscription bundle with human review behind the alerts. Softwr lists it under Manufacturing. MOVUS is available on Web, iOS, Android.
...
MOVUS is a Brisbane company whose FitMachine product is a magnetically mounted wireless sensor measuring vibration, temperature and acoustics on rotating equipment, paired with a cloud platform that scores asset condition and raises alerts. What separates it from a pure sensor vendor is that MOVUS positions the offer as monitoring rather than as software: alerts are reviewed before they reach the customer, so a maintenance team receives a small number of assessed notifications rather than a stream of anomaly scores to triage themselves. The distinguishing capability is hazardous-area coverage. MOVUS released the FitMachine 3XT EX, certified for use in hazardous zones, with availability from February 2026. For mining, oil and gas and processing operations in Australia and South East Asia, an Ex-certified wireless condition monitoring sensor removes the main blocker to instrumenting equipment in classified areas, where the alternative has been cabled systems at many times the cost or no monitoring at all. That certification, and the local presence behind it, is the practical reason this small vendor wins against global competitors on its home ground. Buyers are mining operations, water utilities, food processing and manufacturing sites, predominantly in Australia and New Zealand, with some international presence often reached through insurance and industrial services partners. The trade-off is scale and geography: MOVUS is a small company, coverage and support outside Australasia depend on partners, and per…

