Siemens LOGO! 8 logic modules ship without a native OPC UA stack. The integrated Ethernet port on every LOGO! 8 base module supports only two industrial protocols: S7 communication (over ISO-on-TCP and TCP) and Modbus TCP (server role from firmware FS:04 onward, client role from FS:06 onward). OPC UA Unified Architecture, as specified in IEC 62541 by the OPC Foundation, must therefore be terminated by an external protocol gateway or routed through a cloud broker. This reference documents every documented path between a LOGO! 8 base module and an OPC UA client, with commissioning steps, address-mapping examples, security configuration, and a troubleshooting matrix.
