Connecting an industrial PLC to a cloud-hosted web application requires a deliberate architecture decision because most controller firmware does not natively speak modern web protocols. The PLC was designed for deterministic, real-time I/O scanning over fieldbuses (PROFIBUS, PROFINET), not for serving REST endpoints or streaming telemetry to Kafka. The engineer must therefore choose a transport layer (OPC UA, MQTT, REST), a boundary device (PC, industrial gateway, IIoT edge node), and a security perimeter (DMZ, VPN, TLS mutual auth) before a single byte of application data can flow.
