Process Control
MacroView SCADA/HMI and IIOT Solutions
MacroView SCADA/HMI
MacroView is a SCADA software system widely used in the Coal, Oil, Gas, Mining, Production, Transportation, Environmental and Power Industries. As a specialist SCADA engineering platform, MacroView provides an integrated environment for the acquisition, presentation and analysis of live plant data.
As an advanced human machine interface (HMI), MacroView HMI SCADA is an integrated solution for the acquisition, presentation and analysis of live plant data and events. A fully multitasking and multi-user system, it includes an advanced graphical interface, extensive historian, data logging and reporting capabilities, delivering robust process control and production control systems for the effective operation of production facilities, plants and equipment.
Integrated PLC System & Hardware Control
A SCADA software solution is only as effective as the hardware it communicates with. At Sentient, we specialise in integrating PLC and SCADA architectures to ensure seamless data flow across your entire SCADA network.
Our MacroView SCADA engineering team provides support for your PLC system, including PLC and SCADA integration, ensuring your programmable logic controllers and supervisory control and data acquisition layers work properly. We can also develop PLC HIMI interfaces to allow your operators to monitor hardware performance.
IIoT Solutions and Technology
IoT and IIoT (the Industrial Internet of Things) are rapidly evolving fields of wireless communication connecting a vast array of IIoT devices, ranging from smart sensors to industry-standard rugged transducers and end-user applications. As a leading Perth-based IIoT company, Sentient delivers innovative IIoT technology specifically designed for the Australian industrial landscape.
Our IIoT solutions are built on LoRA technology, using LoRaWAN protocol on the 915MHz Australian frequency band to provide a robust foundation for remote site monitoring and machine monitoring, even in isolated Australian environments.
Proven IIoT Projects in Western Australia
Sentient has successfully deployed multiple IIoT projects throughout WA, showcasing our reliability and industry proficiency. Key features of our IIoT technology deployments include:
Long-Range Connectivity: LoRa has been used to provide long-range wireless communication, crucial for remote site monitoring in geographically dispersed areas, common in Australia.
Secure LoRaWAN-Compliant Local Gateway: Installed to provide secure in-house communication, with the data being kept on the local Control Network and not being forwarded to a cloud-based application. This architecture helps to form a reliable remote site monitoring system.
Advanced Machine Monitoring: LoRaWAN-compliant Class A IIoT devices, including temperature and humidity sensors, pressure-based and ultrasonic level sensors, and vibration machine monitoring sensors. These IIoT devices have a battery life of 5 years and up, and a sampling period of between 10 minutes and an hour has been installed with success, optimised for efficient remote monitoring and RMM (remote monitoring and management).
Dynamic Sampling Rates: For some sensors, an auto update of the sampling rate (to provide quick updates to the operator if the sensor data changes) is enabled. This allows near-real-time updates, valuable for remote site monitoring.
Seamless System Integration: Our IIoT Technology has been integrated with MacroView, currently supervising the whole plant at these locations, to provide machine monitoring and trending facilities. The solution could also be used to provide data directly to most Control Systems or Historians if required. This positions Sentient as a key player among IIoT companies offering comprehensive RMM solutions.
