GET IN TOUCH
FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS
What is IIOT?
IIoT stands for the Industrial Internet of Things. It refers to a network of smart sensors, instruments, and devices connected to industrial applications to monitor, optimise, and automate physical processes.
IIoT is commonly used in mines, refineries, utilities, manufacturing plants, and remote operational sites.
What are the Benefits of IIoT?
IIoT systems provide several key advantages, including:Reduced costs through predictive maintenance and fewer unplanned breakdowns
Increased efficiency and production output with real-time, data-driven decision-making.
Improved safety via continuous monitoring and early detection of issues.
Greater visibility across equipment, remote sites, and processes.
Scalability and remote access reduce the need for on-site intervention.
What is SCADA?
SCADA stands for Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition. It is a combination of hardware and software used to monitor, acquire data from, control, and visualise industrial processes in real time. SCADA helps operators make informed decisions, automate tasks, and keep critical process control and production control systems running safely and efficiently.
Where are SCADA Systems Used?
SCADA systems are used in industries that require continuous monitoring, control, and automation, such as utilities, manufacturing, mining, energy, and infrastructure. By providing real-time insights, automated alerts, and historical data, SCADA helps optimise process control, strengthen production control systems, reduce downtime, and improve safety.
What is HMI?
HMI stands for Human–Machine Interface.
An HMI provides the visual interface that allows operators to interact with a SCADA system—viewing data, acknowledging alarms, and controlling equipment. It is the front-end layer that makes complex industrial systems easy to understand and operate.
In What Industries are Macroview SCADA/HMI Systems Typically Deployed?
MacroView SCADA/HMI systems are deployed in high-intensity, mission-critical environments, including the following:
Mining
Oil & gas
Chemicals and processing
Manufacturing
Utilities (power, water, wastewater)
Transport and logistics
Production and industrial operations
MacroView is designed for harsh conditions, large asset bases, and high-reliability 24/7 environments.
