### During a flare, you can lose fluids and electrolytes faster than plain water alone replaces them 

- Sip steadily through the day rather than trying to catch up with a large amount at once, which the gut may not tolerate well mid-flare
- Oral rehydration solutions replace electrolytes more effectively than water alone during heavier fluid loss
- Broths and soups add fluid, sodium, and a bit of easy nutrition at the same time
- Limit caffeine and alcohol during a flares, as both can act as diuretics and may irritate the digestive system

