Tennessee fully eliminated its income tax (the Hall Tax on investment income) in January 2021 — making it a true zero-income-tax state. Nashville residents pay a Davidson County property tax with an effective rate of approximately 0.70% of appraised value, and Tennessee's combined sales tax in Nashville is 9.75% (7% state + 2.75% county — one of the highest in the US).
