I'm writing this post today, not out of spite, but out of a sense of responsibility to share my experience with upGrad and upGrad Campus. It's crucial for me to bring to light the stark contrast between the promises made and the reality of what is delivered, especially regarding placements and salary expectations.

When I joined upGrad, I was buoyed by the enthusiastic assurances from admission counselors and the team, claiming that upGrad would provide assured placements regardless of background, focusing solely on the skills we would acquire. The narrative was convincing, especially with the promise of an average salary package of around 8 LPA for fresh data scientists, which was a significant factor in my decision to enroll.

However, as the course neared completion, the reality began to starkly contrast with the initial promises. Despite assurances that skill would outweigh background, finding even the most basic placement opportunities became a challenge, let alone ones that matched the promised salary bracket. Technical and non-technical students alike found themselves in a limbo, with opportunities scarce and far removed from the expectations set at the beginning of our journey.

The placement cell, which was supposed to be a robust bridge between us and our future employers, turned out to be a weak link, with very few companies being brought in for placements, most offering salaries as low as 3 LPA - a far cry from the assured 8 LPA.

This situation has not only caused financial strain but also emotional and mental stress, as many of us joined upGrad with the hope of transitioning into rewarding careers in data science and other fields. The reality has been a series of missed opportunities and unfulfilled promises.

I'm writing this post to caution prospective…

