Unpopular opinion: your degree matters far less than your GitHub.
...
I have watched two types of candidates go through ML hiring processes.

Type A: strong university brand, average GitHub, limited real projects.

Type B: average university, strong GitHub, deployed real projects with writeups.

Type B is getting more interviews.
...
Hiring managers for ML roles are mostly ML engineers themselves.

They know what a strong project looks like.

They know what a genuine commit history looks like.

They know the difference between tutorial code and original work.

A GitHub with one messy real project that you clearly struggled through and fixed teaches them more about you than a 9 CGPA from a famous college.

This does not mean degrees are worthless.

It means the premium on top university brands is compressing faster than most students realise.

The kids currently in tier 2 colleges who are building real ML projects publicly are going to out-compete overconfident IITians who have never shipped anything.

