[3] Sharing my honest experience with upGrad’s Digital Marketing course (for awareness) | Junaid Hasan (2026-02-03T00:00:00.000Z)
URL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dmjunaidhasan_sharing-my-honest-experience-with-upgrad-activity-7424432107436949504--Y-0
Before enrolling, I was clearly told by the admission counselor that I would get unlimited 1-on-1 mentor/coach sessions. This was a major reason I chose upGrad.

However, after enrolling, the reality turned out to be very different:

• Only 4–5 TA sessions during the 5-month base program
• Just 1 TA session during the specialization
• Most doubt-solving happens in DDR sessions with 60–80 learners, where 1 hour is clearly insufficient for meaningful support.

The course costs around ₹95,000 for a 6-month program with one compulsory specialization, while similar digital marketing courses are available in the ₹25k–₹30k range elsewhere.

Another major concern was placement expectations. I was told I could get a ₹8–10 LPA job after completion, which is extremely misleading.
In reality, most freshers are offered internships with stipends of ₹6k–₹12k, not high-paying roles.

Now the most frustrating part — specialization policy:

Once a specialization is chosen, it cannot be replaced

I wanted to change (replace) my specialization, but this was outright refused

I was told to pay ₹15,000 extra if I wanted another specialization

This means I’d end up with two specializations, including one I don’t even want — instead of simply replacing it

Despite paying ₹95k, flexibility was not provided.

Additionally, the course content is very basic, offering only introductory-level knowledge of digital marketing.

Overall, this experience has been disappointing and stressful. I personally would not recommend upGrad, and I strongly advise learners to not rely blindly on admission counselors’ promises. Please verify everything in writing before enrolling.

