# India Skills Report 2024

India’s talent outlook to 2030 backed by nationwide assessments and hiring data to decode employability trends and workforce needs.

The India Skills Report 2024 delves into how artificial intelligence is reshaping the future of work, skills, and career mobility in India. Drawing insights from 3.88 lakh candidates who participated in the Wheebox National Employability Test (WNET) and inputs from 152 leading corporations, the report provides a data-backed overview of India’s evolving talent and employability landscape.

This year’s edition highlights the growing demand-supply gap in emerging domains such as AI, machine learning, data science, and DevOps, emphasizing the need for agile and future-oriented skilling. It also presents regional and demographic insights into workforce readiness, identifying which states and age groups are more employable and equipped for the new economy.
