2004). Some workers have specifically focused on the ecological ramifications of the invasion of the water column by small animals to avoid predation on the sea floor (Signor & Vermeij 1994, Peterson et al. 2005), an idea that finds support from the fossil record of pelagic algae, which evolved antipredator defenses in the Early

Cambrian (Butterfield 1997, 2001).
