Efficiency Arizona products are highly efficient appliances, HVAC equipment, and measures to improve energy efficiency, home comfort, and help Arizonans save on their energy bills. Rebates cover a percentage of the total project costs, up to $14,000 per household, depending on income level.

## Heat Pump

A heat pump uses electricity to move heat between the inside and the outside of a building, providing heating and cooling. Heat pumps are more efficient than traditional heating and cooling systems and can cost less to operate.

Eligibility: To be eligible for a heat pump rebate, the household must meet program income eligibility requirements, and property ownership requirements, and the new heat pump must replace an electric furnace, electric baseboard heating, a less efficient heat pump, or be added in addition to an existing HVAC system.

The new heat pump must be a qualifying Energy Star-rated heat pump.

Note: Replacement of a fossil fuel HVAC system with a heat pump is not allowed! Insulation and air sealing may be required alongside the heat pump installation. 

