23-15 Exemptions.

None of the terms or prohibitions of Sections 23-12 through 23-17 shall apply to or be enforced against:

(a)    Any vehicle of the City while engaged upon necessary public business.

(b)    Excavations or repairs of bridges, streets or highways by or on behalf of the City or the State, at
night, when the public welfare and convenience renders it impossible to perform such work during
the day.

(c)    The reasonable use of amplifiers or loudspeakers in the course of public addresses which are
noncommercial in character, and which amplifiers or loudspeakers are not used in connection with
any moving vehicle.

