### Does a heat pump cost more to maintain than a furnace and AC?

Per visit, yes — a heat pump tune-up typically runs $150–$250 versus $80–$150 for a furnace or AC alone, because a heat pump's reversing valve and defrost cycle add inspection points. But a heat pump is one system doing both jobs, so it's usually cheaper overall than maintaining a separate furnace and AC on a combined two-visit contract ($150–$350/year).

