Photo: Getty Images
Triple-digit temperatures have become [the summer norm for some regions](https://www.consumerreports.org/home-garden/weather-safety/how-to-stay-safe-in-a-heat-wave-a3315246736/) of the U.S. Whether or not that’s true in your area, it’s important to pick a central air conditioning system that won’t easily break. Of the nearly two dozen brands judged in CR’s latest member survey, only two stood out with top scores for both predicted reliability and owner satisfaction. Seven additional central air brands earned favorable reliability scores. 
But the data—based on responses from 13,306 members who purchased central AC or ductless mini-split units between 2009 and 2024—suggests that there are many more brands worth considering. There are also some that you should probably pass on if you’re looking to minimize long-term repair and upkeep costs.
 
