To identify systems that are likely to last, Consumer Reports measures and tracks their reliability over extended periods by conducting regular member surveys. Our guide will help you choose the right AC system for your home—and then maintain it so that you can get the unit’s longest life and the best performance possible. We’ll also share some tips on how to find a good heating, ventilating, and air conditioning (HVAC) technician to do the work. 

CR members can see our ratings for the most reliable ducted AC brands based on survey data we’ve collected on more than 13,000 units in real-world use, bought and installed between 2009 and 2024. Our surveys have found that about 19 percent of central AC systems purchased during that timeframe encountered at least one problem. What’s more, 24 percent of those units stopped working as well as they should or altogether, so it can pay to pick a more reliable central air conditioner brand. Through our surveys, we also learned which AC brands owners tend to be most satisfied with, the costs of repairs, and which parts break most often.
...
Reliability Reliability is the second-best predictor for an owner’s overall satisfaction with an air conditioner (tied with how quickly it cools a room, though that has more to do with whether the AC is sized correctly for your home and whether it’s maintained properly). Consumer Reports rates the predicted reliability of 22 central air conditioner brands, based on what members have shared about more than 13,000 new AC units they bought and installed in their own homes between 2009 and 2024.

