[3] Viewing a thread - Quadtrac drive lugs (2023-02-26T00:00:00.000Z)
URL: https://talk.newagtalk.com/forums/thread-view.asp?mid=10113965&tid=1101381
Cracking around the base of the drive lugs is considered normal and does not warrant replacing the track. Missing a single lug is OK, not the best but should not hurt performance. It there are three or more in a row missing the track should be replaced. If there are 4 or more missing anywhere on the track they should be replaced. This is from the Goodyear warranty manual. New Camso tracks are $6500 to $8000 each depending on quality of track and width. Most dealers keep at least one or two on hand. There are times when CNH will run a special for the dealer where they buy a full truckload for a discount that they can pass on to you, usually about $500 per track. Many tire stores that deal with ag tires will have tracks on hand for most tractors. Price ranges depending on quality.

