Preparation for Test 
The tractor is required to have been limbered up by the manufac 
turer for a sufficient number of hours; if this was not done, this lim 
ber-up is performed at the lractor Test Lab. 
Adjustments are permitted during this period. After the start or 
the official test, no adjustments can be made. Any adjustments, re 
pairs, alterations or replacements are mentioned in the final Nebraska 
Tractor l est report. At this time, instrumentation for measuring en 
gine rpm, fan speed, temperatures and pressures is installed on the 
tractor. The tractor is also provided with connections to the Lab's fuel 
supply. 
PTO Performance 
The tractor PTO is connected to a dynamornete1~ which is a device 
for putting a load on the traclor and measuring the power generated 
by the Lractor. During the preliminary runs, Lhe manufacturer is al 
lowed to make some adjustments to optimize the performance. These 
adjustments, which include the injection pump volume and timing 
and the high idle set within the specified range, will remain during 
the whole test program and must be settings guaranteed by the manu 
facturer. 
The Lests are performed while maintaining an ambient tempera 
ture or 73°F (23°C) and at a barometer reading above 28.5 inches 
