Nebraska Tractor Test Results | Case IH
Company
Efficient Power
Nebraska Test Results
Back
Nebraska Test Results
The Case IH Steiger® 620 tractor sets new performance records in fluid-efficient power, drawbar horsepower and maximum pull in recent tests at the Nebraska Tractor Test Laboratory.
Wheeled or Tracked — The Steiger 620 Sets New Performance Records
In tests at the Nebraska Tractor Test Laboratory (NTTL), the Steiger Quadtrac1 620 tractor set new records for drawbar fuel efficiency, drawbar horsepower and maximum pull, not long after the Steiger 620 wheeled tractor did the same — outperforming all models ever tested.2 With the world's most fluid-efficient and highest drawbar horsepower tractors in your fleet, it won't be long before you're setting new records on your operation, too. Not to mention, you can experience more efficiency, reduced maintenance and lower operating costs thanks to patented Case IH SCR emission technology. Get more with Steiger tractors.
Full Wheeled Results
Full Quadtrac Results
Steiger 620 Wheeled Tractor Performance
Drawbar Fuel Efficiency
Patented Case IH SCR technology is simply the most efficient and most powerful diesel emissions-control technology there is. With no particulate filter to clean, no regeneration period and 600 operating hours between oil changes, on average, Steiger tractors cost up to $1,000 less per year to own and maintain than comparable John Deere® models.3
Drawbar Horsepower
It's one thing to generate a lot of horsepower. It's another to efficiently transfer that power throughout the tractor and to the ground and the implement you're pulling. With 37 more usable horsepower, that’s exactly the type of performance you can expect from the Steiger 620 wheeled tractor.
Maximum Pull
The Steiger 620 wheeled tractor handles more weight than any tractor ever tested by the NTTL. That means you can work with the largest implements available and cover more acres on your operation, more efficiently per day. Plus, separately activated front and rear automatic differential locks help you maintain control even through the toughest pulling conditions.
Steiger 620 Quadtrac Tractor Performance
Drawbar Fuel Efficiency
Patented Case IH SCR technology allows the engine to run cleaner, which extends oil change intervals — 600 hours for Case IH versus 450 hours for most competitive units —reducing operating costs and helping to keep maintenance lower.
Drawbar Horsepower
It's one thing to generate a lot of horsepower. It's another to efficiently transfer that power throughout the tractor, to the ground and the implement you're pulling. That's exactly the type of performance you can expect from the Steiger Quadtrac 620 tractor. With nearly 13 additional horsepower at the drawbar, you can cover more acres in a day and withstand tough conditions whether tilling, seeding or simply pulling a grain cart.
Maximum Pull
The Steiger 620 quadtrac handles more weight than any tractor tested by the NTTL. That means you can work with the largest implements available and cover more acres on your operation, more efficiently per day. An industry-exclusive, separately activated front and rear automatic differential locks help you maintain control even through the toughest pulling conditions.
Best-in-Class Tractors Across the Lineup
Whether in the lab or in the field — where it really matters — the complete Steiger tractor lineup (370, 420, 470, 500, 540, 580, and 620 models) features best-in-class power, torque and fluid efficiency. For example, the wheeled Steiger 580 tractor scored the second-highest drawbar fuel economy ever recorded* at 17.53 horsepower hours per gallon — 6.63 percent higher than the tested competition in its power class.4
Explore Steiger Series
Advantages of Steiger Tractors
Proven SCR emissions technology allows Case IH engines to run cleaner and cooler for better fluid efficiency, including diesel fuel and Diesel Exhaust Fluid (DEF).
More usable horsepower allows you to pull extra implement widths, making you even more productive in the field.
Tri-point oscillation provides the perfect mix of strength and balance when transferring power to the ground, from tillage and planting to nutrient placement and land leveling.
Heavy-duty components are engineered to stand up to the toughest jobs and heaviest loads: durable frame built of ½-inch-thick steel, heavier drivelines, 5.5-inch axles and a long wheelbase with built-in weight.
The power pin drawbar quick hitch automatically connects to your implement so you can hook up and go.
Massive axles carry up to 66,000 pounds of gross vehicle-operating weight.
Industry-exclusive, separately activated front and rear automatic differential locks help you maintain control even through the toughest pulling conditions.
Structural steel fuel tank adds additional weight and strength to the Steiger chassis.
Nebraska Tractor Test Laboratory
The Nebraska Tractor Test Laboratory (NTTL) is the officially designated tractor testing station for the United States and tests tractors according to the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) codes. Twenty-nine countries around the world adhere to the tractor test codes, with nearly all maintaining an active test station. (Photo credit: Meredith Agrimedia)
