ETP18 is a survey database on the key characteristics of platform economy activities and platform workers' perceptions in Argentina in 2018, produced by the Inter-American Development Bank (IDB) for the publication Platform Economy and Employment: What Is It Like to Work for an App in Argentina? Digital platforms have been a major global disruption in the world of work for nearly a decade and are relatively new in Argentina, where the entry of new platforms and foreign subsidiaries accelerated from 2016 onward.
...
The survey was conducted with workers from 11 selected platforms: Mercado Libre, Airbnb, Uber, Cabify, Zolvers, Ando, Glovo, Rappi, Workana, Freelancer and IguanaFix. The database comprises a sample of 603 cases.
...
A triangulation of selection strategies was used because workers on different platforms were not equally easy to reach. The sample was non-probabilistic, and the number of respondents per platform was set using uniform quotas that took into account the accessibility of workers for each platform. Because the sample is non-probabilistic, results should be interpreted as exploratory rather than as statistically representative of all platform workers in Argentina.
...
The dataset supports research and policy analysis on the digital economy, digital platforms, labor markets and formal labor in Argentina and Latin America and the Caribbean. It is distributed as an XLSX database accompanied by a PDF metadata sheet.

