Fair Contracts: This principle assesses whether platform contracts are transparent, accessible, and fair, and whether they protect workers from disproportionate risk. To earn the first point, platforms must ensure that workers can easily understand, access, and agree to their contracts. Contracts must not undermine existing legal protections, and platforms must apply responsible and ethical data protection practices through documented policies. To earn a second point, platforms must ensure that contractual risks and liabilities are fairly shared. This requires advance notice of contract changes without undermining accrued rights, avoiding clauses that exclude platform liability or block workers’ access to legal remedies, monitoring subcontractors’ compliance with platform standards, and ensuring transparency in algorithmic systems that affect pay, ratings, bonuses, or job allocation.
