In the upcoming text revision of the fifth edition of the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-5-TR), the diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder is revised from the DSM-5 diagnosis. In addition to text changes throughout the disorder’s description, which reflect updated literature and advances in knowledge, the most noticeable change is to the diagnostic criteria, specifically criterion A.
