Thank you for the letter regarding the National Committee on Vital and Health Statistics’ (NCVHS) recommendations regarding a central coordinating entity for planning and adopting International Classification of Diseases, Version 11 (ICD-11) in the United States. The Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) appreciates the Committee’s work and recommendations over the past several years regarding ICD-11. We recognize the value of coordination in efforts where multiple governmental entities are involved. I appreciate hearing from you about this important issue.

The Committee recommends that HHS designate one office or agency to be responsible for overall coordination of ICD-11 morbidity coding in the United States and while in the process of organizing a coordinating office or agency, appoint a federal representative to the World Health Organization as it considers comprehensive coordination of morbidity coding. Given the significant implications for updating the ICD-10 code set, HHS will review these recommendations and consider them at the appropriate time and then work with other agencies regarding a transition to ICD-11 to determine the best path forward.

