The WHO crosswalk used on this page is the official forward mapping from ICD-10-CM to ICD-11 MMS (Mortality and Morbidity Statistics). Each entry is classified as equivalent, narrower, broader, or approximate based on the degree to which the two codes share clinical scope. Equivalent mappings allow direct substitution. Narrower mappings indicate that ICD-11 is more granular and that the coder should verify clinical detail before selecting the target. Broader mappings indicate that ICD-11 aggregates conditions that ICD-10 distinguished separately.

