# Indian Residential Schools Settlement Agreement 

 This document is the Indian Residential Schools Settlement Agreement, dated May 8, 2006, between Canada, plaintiffs represented by the National Consortium and the Merchant Law Group, Independent Counsel, the Assembly of First Nations and Inuit Representatives, and various church organizations. The agreement aims for a fair, comprehensive, and lasting resolution to the legacy of Indian Residential Schools by settling class actions, providing common experience payments, establishing an independent assessment process, creating a Truth and Reconciliation Commission, and funding healing programs and commemoration efforts. It outlines the terms and conditions under which claims related to Indian Residential Schools will be settled.

