Between 2010 and 2015, the Tribunal systematically reported on its performance and activities to the Security Council and the General Assembly, and made steady progress in monitoring its judicial activities. The Tribunal also implemented a number of operational and procedural reforms, and monitored them, in order to achieve the completion strategy. The Tribunal accomplished this in the context of implementing a downsizing exercise, during which it experienced a 53 per cent decrease in its overall workforce in the five-year temporal scope examined. At the same time, evidence on demonstrating performance results proved elusive. While there were different perspectives on how to interpret the dates of the completion strategy, there was also an absence of clear indicators to enable a transparent assessment of the extent to which the completion of work was on track. Measures of effectiveness and efficiency were based largely on…

