Through Which Mechanisms Do Human Rights Prosecutions affect Repression? Once we establish if human rights prosecutions are associated with improvements in human rights, we need to ask about the mechanisms through which these improvements occur. One key literature on mechanisms is the rational choice literature on the causes of repression. This literature argues that state officials choose repression because the benefits gained from repression exceed the costs (Poe, 2004). From this point of view, the expected benefits of repression may include the political gains for repressing political opponents, and the financial gains of expropriating…

