1. This case relates to crimes against humanity and war crimes which took place between August 2003 and March 2004, in Darfur, Sudan. The Sudan situation was referred to the International Criminal Court by the UN Security Council (Resolution 1593) on 31 March 2005. Whilst, as is well-known, arrest warrants were issued for other leading actors in that conflict in Darfur, the trial of this Accused, (who surrendered himself in 2020), is the only one which has taken place. The evidence given by the many innocent civilians, mainly from the Fur tribe, who were victims of the grave and undisputed crimes, has revealed the suffering they underwent at the time, which still continues to-day. This trial has for the first time allowed them a voice with which to inform the world of what happened to them as a result of this conflict.

