You also have to verify the transactions reported or corrected by all your Fairtrade business partners (suppliers, customers).
...
• In order to report or verify a transaction, you need to connect with your business partners. Do so by inviting them to connect with you or by accepting their invite. 
• Only report or verify completed transactions, where the product was delivered and the Fairtrade Price (and Premium, if relevant) were already paid. 
• For your product reporting, use the product codes available on the platform. If you do not fi nd your product, please contact us at reporting@fl ocert.net so we can add it. 
• If you are responsible for paying or conveying the Fairtrade Price and/or Premium (i.e you are a Payer or Conveyer in the Fairtrade Standards) you need to include information about the Price and Premium paid when you do your reporting. 
• If you are reporting fi nal Fairtrade product sales in the platform Connect, you do not have to report these sales into Fairtrace as well. 
• If you have not had any Fairtrade transactions in the period you are reporting for or you are not the reporting party, choose “Nothing to report” in your report declarations. 

