The Fairtrade Minimum Price Differential is the difference between the Fairtrade Minimum Price (FMP) and the national reference price in Cote d'Ivoire and Ghana, as indicated in the Cocoa Fairtrade Standard 4.2.1. The Standard requires trader s to pay a price differential for Fairtrade cocoa beans if national reference prices in these countries fall below the FMP. This mechanism ensures that the price the producer s receive is not below the FMP.
