Uganda. In future, our international buyers need to prove that the coffee they import is produced legally, sustainably, and has not caused deforestation on your farm. With your registration, you make it possible to show this to your buyers.

What is coffee traceability? Coffee traceability is a trading method that tracks coffee from the farm where it is produced to a consumer who drinks it and vice versa. This is done by attaching a farm identifier to the coffee when it is sold by the farmer. The farm identifier travels with the coffee through the value chain to the consumer. In practice, most of this is done digitally (on smartphones and computers). A traceability system requires a place where coffee farmer and farm data are stored and a traceability application that links the production farm identifier to the traded coffee.
