For a coffee buyer in 2026, the EU Deforestation Regulation is no longer a distant compliance theme. The 30 December 2026 deadline for large and medium operators is eight months away. Penalties include fines of at least 4% of annual EU-wide turnover, plus confiscation of the consignment and the revenues from its sale.

The 2025/2650 amendment carved out two narrow concessions. Micro and small primary operators established before 31 December 2024 have until 30 June 2027 — six extra months. Downstream operators (those buying from an upstream EU operator rather than placing coffee on the EU market themselves) can rely on the upstream DDS reference number rather than submitting their own. For a major roaster, trader or importer, neither carve-out applies. The 30 December 2026 deadline is the working assumption.
