Pai is one of the most special towns in northern Thailand. Nestled in a mountain valley in Mae Hong Son province, it has a unique personality — a blend of tribal culture, international bohemian spirit and lush nature. Its rice fields, waterfalls, hot springs and the famous Pai Canyon make it one of the country's most photogenic destinations. And the Walking Street night market, literally next to the hostel, is the social heart of the town.

What makes Pai special is its pace of life. Without the crowds of Bangkok or Chiang Mai, time passes slowly here between mountain-view cafés, motorbike rides through rice paddies, hot spring soaks and sunsets over the valley. A destination that captures your heart and is hard to leave.
