[2] Chang Bar | KhaosanRoad.com
URL: https://www.khaosanroad.com/places/chang-bar
Casual Khao San pit stop for icy Chang longnecks, easy buckets, and A‑plus people‑watching. Cheap, cheerful, and perfect for a top‑up before the bigger rooms kick off.
...
Chang Bar is the sort of no-fuss streetside spot Khao San does best: plastic stools under fairy lights, cold longnecks sweating on the table, and a steady soundtrack of chart hits and Thai rock rolling out to the lane. It’s the place you duck into between Rambuttri and Khao San for an easy drink and prime people‑watching while the night warms up. Drinks are straightforward and friendly on the wallet. Expect icy Chang and Leo by the bottle, simple mixed drinks, and those shareable buckets that fuel half the street. Prices are the usual Khao San range — roughly 100–120 THB for a beer, buckets from around 250–350 THB — so you can settle in without doing currency gymnastics. Service is quick, smiles come easy, and there’s always a spare stool appearing from somewhere when your crew grows by two. Come by after 8pm when the lane gets lively, or swing through later for a top‑up before the bigger rooms kick off. It’s casual, cheerful, and very Khao San: grab a seat, clink bottles, and let the night stroll past your table.

