On March 31, 2025, Mr. Anan Pothinimdaeng, Deputy Governor of the State Railway of Thailand (SRT), revealed that the SRT Board of Directors meeting on March 27, 2025, approved the use of a flat fare of 20 baht for the entire Red Line suburban railway project (Bang Sue-Rangsit and Bang Sue-Taling Chan) and the Suvarnabhumi Airport Rail Link (ARL) project. This will be implemented from September 2025 onwards for a period of one year.
...
As for the Airport Rail Link, it will join the operation with a flat fare of 20 baht for the entire line starting in September 2025. Currently, the operator is Asia Era One Co., Ltd., which is the concessionaire for the three-airport rail link project (Don Mueang - Suvarnabhumi - U-Tapao).
...
In this regard, the Department of Rail Transport (DRT) is the one who sets the operating principles for the SRT's electric trains, which is the same model that will be used for the MRT Yellow and Pink Lines, which must pay the fare with a registered EMV card. The SRT will summarize and present it to the Ministry of Transport to present to the Cabinet for approval in August 68 before starting the 20-baht electric trains on all routes throughout the line in September 68 in a new format via EMV cards.

Currently, income and expenses from the Airport Link still belong to the SRT, which is still operating at a loss. Compensation is calculated based on the amount of income that has decreased because in the future the private sector will take over operations according to the terms of the joint investment contract. The Airport Link has an average fare of 9.6 baht per person-trip, while the Red Line has an average fare of 10 baht per person-trip, which must be compensated.
