Doi Inthanon is one of Thailand's most famous national parks and also home to Thailand's highest mountain Doi Inthanon. The day tour will start when we depart Chiang Mai and make our way out of the city, after one hour we will turn off the main highway where the road will start to make its way up into the national park. Our first stop of the day will be to see Wachiritharn Waterfall, this high cascading falls have a good flow of water all year and its a great introduction to some of the great sites in this national park. Following Wachiritharn Waterfall we will continue our way up further towards Doi Inthanon's peak, we will make stops at The Royal Agricultural Project and then onto the two iconic Royal Pagodas which are situated high up near Inthanon's peak. Cloud allowing you can get some stunning views over the park from this high vantage point by these pagodas. We will then make our way to the peak of Doi Inthanon at 2565 meters, this its Thailand's highest point and Thailand's highest mountain. At the top of the mountain the air can be very cool (sometime very cold) and is home to a very distinct variety of flora which are not found at lower levels in Thailand this flora can be enjoyed on the short Ankha nature trail which is situated at the top of the mountain. On our way down the mountain we will make further stops at small hill tribe market, a Karen village (not Long neck) at a further waterfall (Siritharn) before making our way back to Chiang Mai and transfer to your hotel.
