### By train

The cheapest and most scenic way of reaching Ayutthaya is by train. These run throughout the day from Bangkok via Don Mueang, taking about 80 min to 2 hours. Ordinary third-class trains (no air-con, unreserved seats) still leave from historic Hua Lamphong and cost about 15 baht. Many faster long-distance trains leave from Krung Thep Aphiwat (Bang Sue), the main northern/northeastern terminus: about 20 baht for third-class on a "rapid" train (no air-con, no reserved seat); 65 baht for an ordinary reserved seat (no air-con); 245 baht for a "rapid" air-con reserved seat; and 345 baht for special express with air-con, a meal, and a reserved seat. In rush hour the trains are horribly overcrowded, but the rush is inward to Bangkok - daytrippers coming outward will dodge this.…

