Mae Kampong is a mountain village in a forested valley about an hour east of Chiang Mai, in Mae On district. Wooden houses cluster along a stream that tumbles through a tiered waterfall, coffee and miang (fermented tea) grow on the surrounding slopes, and the whole place runs as a community-based tourism project. It’s free to visit (you pay only for a coffee, a homestay or an activity) and it’s one of the north’s most rewarding day trips or overnight escapes.
