| System configuration | Plausible wall-power idle range | What usually drives the result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Single-socket workstation with SSD, modest memory, and no discrete GPU | 35–70 W | Motherboard, memory, PSU losses, fans, and chipset |
| Single-socket server with several DIMMs, fans, and storage | 50–100 W | Registered ECC memory, drive electronics, cooling, and controllers |
| Dual-socket tower or server with both CPUs installed | 70–130 W | Second socket, additional memory, interconnect, VRMs, and fans |
| Dual-socket rack server with many DIMMs, a backplane, or PCIe cards | 100–180+ W | Enterprise cooling policy, drives, HBA or RAID, NICs, and redundant PSUs |
| CPU package reported by a monitoring tool | Not comparable to wall power | Usually excludes much of the motherboard, memory, storage, fans, and PSU losses |
