The SPECworkstation ® 4.0 benchmark, released on December 5, 2024, is a major update to SPEC’s comprehensive benchmark designed to measure key aspects of workstation performance.

SPECworkstation 4.0 provides a robust, real-world measure of workstation performance, ensuring that professionals have the data they need to make informed decisions about their hardware investments. The benchmark targets the diverse needs of engineers, scientists, and developers who rely on workstation hardware for daily tasks by including a comprehensive set of tests. A complete benchmark run estimates system performance by measuring 23 workloads and over 80 subtests to generate scores for seven industry verticals and four hardware subsystems.
...
The SPECworkstation 4.0 benchmark reports top-level scores in two categories: industry verticals and hardware subsystems. Individual subtest scores are also reported for users interested in specific workloads. Published results are available to users for comparison.
