That type of high humidity is great for a singing voice but not for any type of elect. gear especially mics. If AC is available and the temp is generally high enough to keep it running you should be able to manage a level in the 50% range. However if that is not the case get some 1 gallon plastic sealable food bags and a bunch of silica keep dry packets (that come with almost every new mic) and put each mic in a bag with a "dried out" packet and seal it up. Heating up the packets in an oven will dry them out pretty well. This way exposure to relative humidity will only occur to the mic pouch that is opened and a fresh packet can be put in the bag with the mic when the gig is over. Hugh
