## Formatting SD cards on the PodTrak P8
**IMPORTANT**: Formatting an SD card will erase all of the data, so make sure to back up any important files beforehand.
Before you can begin recording with your Zoom PodTrak P8, you will need to format the SD card so it can be recognized and function properly. Follow these steps to format the Zoom PodTrak P8 SD card.
1. Insert the SD card then power on your P8. Inserting and ejecting SD cards while the unit is turned on can result in data loss.
2. Tap the**SD Card**icon on the top of the touchscreen display.
3. Tap**Format**, then tap**Format**again when a message appears.
Test SD cards for compatibility
**NOTE:**Zoom recommends the following Class 10 SD cards for recording:
...
There’s no official SD card compatibility list for the P8, but you can perform a quick test to determine whether or not you’ll be able to use it or not. Performing a test is also a good troubleshooting step if you’re receiving errors or if your SD card is performing poorly.
1. Tap the**SD Card**icon on the top of the touchscreen display.
2. Tap**Test**, tap**Quick Test**, then select**Execute**.
3. Once it’s completed, you should see**OK**displayed on the screen.
* The test should only last approximately 30-45 seconds.
Card protected error
If you insert the SD card into the Zoom PodTrak P8 and see a*Card protected*message on the display, take the card out of the P8 and check the security tab on the SD card. If the switch is set to protected mode, the SD card is “locked” so no data can be stored onto it.
