Plenty of podcast studios use only a fraction of their RØDECaster Pro II: they record a stereo mix, plug in a mic, and miss the two features that change everything, in post and on air, namely multitrack recording and automatic mix-minus. This guide explains how to set them up, why they matter, and the settings you need to know so you are not stuck in the edit.
